{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdYAFqZMrqMSaafBMXp1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anthropic's financials, shared with investors this week, show an operating profit in the second quarter and 900% net revenue retention, according to TechCrunch. The article defines the second figure as spending from the same customers in Q3 2025 growing nine times by Q3 2026. Because it tracks existing customers only, it shows how much more they are paying, which is a different quantity from how much they are getting.\n\nThe article places the retention number next to other evidence that spend is climbing. Jellyfish reports that spending on agentic coding tools among its customers has grown 10x since the start of the year, reaching about 2% of total engineering cost, and that Claude Code and other tools built on Anthropic models account for nearly a third of proposed code changes submitted for review. TechCrunch also notes that most of the Fortune 500 are not seeing major gains from deploying AI. Growing spend and unclear returns can exist at the same time, and in this account they do.\n\nThat tension explains the reporting tools Anthropic announced Wednesday. They give managers a view of what a team produced for a given cost over a given period, along with recommendations, drawing on internal analytics and employee surveys. For a company whose growth depends on existing customers continuing to expand, the ability to show what that spending buys supports the number investors are watching. Whether it also answers the questions customers are asking depends on what the reports show once teams start using them, and the article does not report any results yet."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":883,"cache_read_input_tokens":6250,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":883},"